# Platform Guide (Agent Reference)

**Canonical doc:** `apps/docs/core/platform-guide.md`

When you add or change features, **update that file** in the same change — especially the Changelog table and any section describing the behavior you touched. Mirror condensed facts here.

## Goal

Train an ML surrogate that predicts an RCC column's load–deformation response (peak and/or full backbone) from design parameters. Validate against PEER experiments; optionally reuse ANSYS runs in the same schema.

## Data sources

| Source | Role |
|--------|------|
| PEER UW rectangular DB | Experimental specimens (~299) |
| ANSYS exports | Numerical runs; same columns + `source=ansys` |
| `data/raw/properties_rect.csv` | Feature table (one row per specimen) |

## Modelling modes

| Mode | Row | X → y | Output files |
|------|-----|--------|--------------|
| Peak | one specimen | design params → `peak_load_kN` (+ optional `disp_at_peak_mm`) | `dataset_ml.csv`, `best_model_peak.joblib` |
| Curve | one curve point | design params + `displacement_mm` → `lateral_load_kN` | `curves_backbone.csv`, `best_model_curve.joblib` |

Start with **peak**, then **curve**. Always split by `specimen` / `specimen_id`.

## Feature columns (properties)

`specimen`, `fc_MPa`, `P_axial_kN`, `b_mm`, `h_mm`, `L_mm`, `Lsplice_mm`, `test_config`, `db_long_mm`, `n_long_bars`, `cover_mm`, `rho_long`, `fyl_MPa`, `steel_grade`, `db_trans_mm`, `s_hoop_mm`, `rho_trans`, `fyt_MPa`, `failure_mode`, `axial_load_ratio`, optional `source`

Units: SI only (mm, kN, MPa).

## Streamlit UI tabs (`apps/web/`)

| Surface | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| Predict (home) | Design-param form → peak + curve prediction |

No navbar; Models/Curves not in the app shell.

## Models (baselines)

Random Forest, XGBoost, MLP — pick best by **group CV RMSE** (not test R² alone); classify fit scenarios per `ml-evaluation.mdc`.

## Hosting

Private GitHub + Streamlit Community Cloud (`apps/web/streamlit_app.py`). Track `best_model_*.joblib` for deploy. Push → auto redeploy. Guide: `apps/docs/guides/hosting.md`.

